From: pyramid <pyramid@tempo.xyz>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:44:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(certify): print a statement's hash premises, check
 footprints

check_final prints every keccak256 premise the published statement
rests on (PREMISE scoped|global|refuted ...), unfolding its
definitions, and refuses a statement resting on a premise Lean proves
false. footprint.py decides each scoped premise for the real keccak256
in the kernel at concrete calls; the driver runs it after check_final
and records the instances as the hash_premise status.
